<article class="legal-page-wrapper">
  <div class="legal-page-container">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <span class="legal-pill">Legal &amp; Compliance</span>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Last Updated: September 19, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="card glass-panel legal-card">
      <div class="legal-prose">
        <p>
          At <strong>Digvolly</strong>, accessible from <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">{{ shop.name | default: 'Digvolly' }}</a>, we are committed to protecting the privacy and personal information of our customers and visitors. This Privacy Policy outlines what data we collect, how it is used, how it is safeguarded, and your individual rights regarding your information.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>When you browse our store, create an account, or purchase digital design assets, we collect certain information to provide and improve our service:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact Information:</strong> Your name, email address, billing address, and account login details.</li>
          <li><strong>Order &amp; Transaction Details:</strong> Products purchased, license keys, purchase date, order total, and payment confirmation status. (We do <em>not</em> store full credit card numbers; payments are processed securely by PCI-compliant payment gateways).</li>
          <li><strong>Device &amp; Usage Information:</strong> IP address, browser type, operating system, referring URLs, pages viewed, and session timestamps collected automatically via standard server logs.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>Your personal data is used solely for legitimate business purposes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Order Fulfillment &amp; Delivery:</strong> Generating your instant ZIP download links and delivering permanent file backup links to your email address.</li>
          <li><strong>Customer Support:</strong> Responding to inquiries, troubleshooting file extraction or software compatibility questions, and providing license verification.</li>
          <li><strong>Account Management:</strong> Maintaining your purchase history so you can re-download acquired assets at any time.</li>
          <li><strong>Marketing Communications (Optional):</strong> Sending free design drops and product release updates only if you have explicitly opted in. You can unsubscribe at any time using the link in any marketing email.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
        <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal data. We partner only with trusted third-party service providers who assist us in operating our marketplace under strict confidentiality agreements:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Shopify Inc.:</strong> Our e-commerce platform host. Your data is stored securely through Shopify’s data storage, databases, and general application architecture.</li>
          <li><strong>Payment Processors:</strong> Stripe, PayPal, Apple Pay, and Google Pay for encrypted payment authorization. All processors adhere to PCI-DSS Level 1 security standards.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloud Infrastructure &amp; CDN:</strong> Fast delivery networks for high-speed master file downloads and image previews.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Cookies &amp; Tracking Technologies</h2>
        <p>
          We use cookies and similar technologies to remember your shopping cart items, recognize your browser across sessions, analyze catalog traffic, and improve storefront performance. You can manage or disable cookies in your browser settings at any time, though disabling cookies may affect your ability to keep items in your cart.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Data Retention &amp; Security</h2>
        <p>
          We retain order data indefinitely so you can exercise lifetime access to your digital downloads. We employ 256-bit SSL encryption across the entire store, industry-standard firewalls, and rigorous administrative controls to safeguard your data against unauthorized access, loss, or alteration.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Your Data Rights (GDPR / CCPA)</h2>
        <p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Request a copy of the personal information we hold about you.</li>
          <li>Request corrections to any inaccurate or incomplete personal data.</li>
          <li>Request the deletion or anonymization of your personal data (subject to legal and tax retention requirements).</li>
          <li>Opt out of marketing communications at any time.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Contact Information</h2>
        <p>
          If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, your data, or wish to submit a data request, please contact our privacy team:
        </p>
        <div class="legal-callout">
          <strong>Digvolly Privacy Office</strong><br>
          Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@digvolly.com">privacy@digvolly.com</a> or <a href="/pages/contact">Studio Support</a><br>
          Response Time: Within 24–48 business hours.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Privacy Policy",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
